// diet plan for like each individual"; docs/RECIPE_PERSONAS_2026-11-26.md): vegan, Jain and vegetarian lunches and dinners with the most protein the everyday kinds allow.
// Every ingredient is an everyday kind or one of the protein kinds a small shop stocks (tofu, Quorn, soya drink: lib/mm/localRangeProtein.ts); see
// lib/mm/recipeBook/index.ts for the rules every recipe follows.
// - Vegan and tofu-led, written at about 550 to 650 kcal a serving with the tofu (and chickpeas) as the protein and the rice, pasta, bread or wraps as a side the
//   plan can halve or double, so the same dish fits a small protein-first meal and a big training-day one.
// - Vegan with no soya (no tofu, soy sauce or bread): chickpeas, kidney beans and peanut butter carry it.
// - Jain (no onion, garlic, roots, mushrooms, eggs or honey, nor the made sauces, pastes, powders and stock cubes that print onion or garlic): tofu, cottage
//   cheese, yogurt, cheese, chickpeas, kidney beans, peanut butter and almonds, with cumin, turmeric, paprika, cinnamon, oregano, herbs, black pepper and lemon.
//   They suit "No onion or garlic" too.
// - No gluten (rice), and vegetarian lunches with no eggs.

